  "id": "COMPOUND:27136 - PROTEIN:1442",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 8-acetoxy T-2 tetraol may act as a target for multiple molecular entities that ultimately lead to the DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. This relationship is supported by the presence of 8-acetoxy T-2 tetraol as a target for Sphingosine 1-phosphate receptor 4 and Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 8, both of which are themselves targets of other compounds. These intermediates then direct their activity toward DNA polymerase alpha subunit B, indicating a potential pathway where 8-acetoxy T-2 tetraol may serve as a bridge or modulator in the signaling or metabolic processes that influence DNA polymerase activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for 8-acetoxy T-2 tetraol in regulating DNA polymerase alpha subunit B through indirect interactions, possibly via receptor-mediated signaling or metabolic activation.",
